WEBVTT

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.390
<i>Analyzing incoming visuals.</i>

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:25.310
We have a match.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:32.860
<i>I want to remind you that</i>

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.150
these men are criminals, but they're
also crucial material witnesses.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:40.200
<i>It's imperative</i>
<i>that they're captured unharmed. Got it?</i>

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.120
James, they're heading into the crowd!

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:11.940
Shit.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:25.660
The fool.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:37.710
Don't fire!

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:46.640
I knew it.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.930
That bastard took a GPS round
without asking.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:57.320
Shit.

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.780
James, the main street.
I'll forward the location.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:12.160
It'll be about 10 minutes if I leave now.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.630
<i>-Hey!</i>
<i>-I'm borrowing this.</i>

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:18.960
Hey!

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:31.600
Is he going to ram him?

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:38.820
Shit!

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:19.980
They're headed for the crowd!

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:50.220
This is James Blood.

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:55.270
Mission complete.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:57.980
Damn, I'm freezing.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:01.020
Oh, that's warm.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:03.150
Oh, the hero's back!

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.450
Heard you fired off your gun!

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:09.360
-Here comes the hotshot!
-Hey!

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:13.700
-I don't want to hear it.
-You took equipment again.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:16.200
-Coming back from a triathlon?
-I won!

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:19.000
You're the laughing stock of the station.

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:23.500
--doesn't mean it's okay!

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:27.420
You're not supposed to fire your gun
without clearance.

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:30.220
That's enough already.
Why are you on my case--?

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:34.930
-What I'm saying is--
-I can't hear you because of the water.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:37.640
And the GPS round you fired

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:40.650
-is something I developed.
-Oh, James.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.650
-People will think I had a part in it.
-You got to a sauna?

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:45.650
It worked out, so what's the problem?

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:47.240
No, it didn't.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:53.950
-I'm telling you this for your own sake.
-Keep it to yourself.

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:55.950
What are you doing after this?

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:00.120
I'm going to get my things and go home
before he finds me.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.670
Before he finds you? What are you--?

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:07.960
Welcome back.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.640
You should've left before he found you.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:33.570
<i>When asked about the bribery allegations</i>
<i>made against LIVE Corporation,</i>

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:38.870
<i>the company's chairman, Steven Martland,</i>
<i>stated that the reports are baseless--</i>

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.290
Did you not know?

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.540
You're not supposed to hurt
material witnesses.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.630
I think you saw
that I had no other choice--

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:50.800
Why did you fire your gun
without permission?

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:54.800
I always tell you not to jump the gun.

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:57.810
-But I had no choice in that situation--
-Also...

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:03.060
You had a choice when you took equipment
from the station without the paperwork.

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:07.070
-James, how many years have you been here?
-Seven years.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.570
Yes, it will be eight years.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:13.740
You should know what kind of organization
we're running here by now.

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:18.490
<i>This is a police organization</i>

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:21.830
<i>responsible for</i>
<i>maintaining peace and order in society.</i>

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:25.330
And we are the bureau in charge
of the dangerous cases

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:29.250
-which require careful countermeasures.
-Which require careful countermeasures.

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:31.630
That is our job at the SSC.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:40.220
Everyone here recognizes your abilities.
Your clearance rate is off the charts.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:44.520
It brings me pride as a fellow SSC member.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:46.600
-Thank you, sir.
-However!

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:51.320
Reckless actions puts others in danger.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:55.660
I called you in here because I'd like you
to do something about that.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:01.330
The SSC is an organization in which
you are an individual member.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.160
Yes, sir...

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:09.130
Here's the paperwork.
You get to fill it out.

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:14.720
It's been 30 years since our founding.

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:20.430
Our work has greatly evolved
over the years.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:24.430
Our tasks and responsibilities expanded

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:27.900
along with the transfer of authority
ten years ago.

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:31.020
I believe this present case
exemplifies this.

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:36.150
We, the prosecution, need to understand
our citizens now more than ever.

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:47.960
This is all the documented evidence?

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:49.540
I...

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:52.630
I didn't know.

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:58.840
I didn't know that research
would lead to this.

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:02.810
So...

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:04.680
The professor is...?

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:09.810
I prepared myself
when you first reached out to me.

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:11.360
I'm sorry...

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:14.610
for dragging you into this dangerous mess.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:16.440
It's fine.

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:19.570
I can't turn back now.

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:24.660
I'm putting you under our protection.

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:27.080
Do you understand what that means?

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:31.330
Are you prepared to take the stand?

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:37.470
You don't need to worry about that.
This can't be allowed to go unpunished.

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:39.340
And one more thing:

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:43.180
I will be requesting help from
someone in the SSC for this case.

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:45.180
The SSC...

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:47.810
Can they be trusted?

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:52.110
Yes, he can be trusted.

00:10:57.030 --> 00:10:57.860
Thank you.

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:03.370
A number of these reports mentioned
the prosecution. Does that mean...?

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:06.620
You'll likely be working
with Monica again.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:12.130
Monica? I feel like
we're always asking for her help.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:18.010
That is her job, after all.
It's actually more like her hobby.

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:40.570
Monica?

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:46.580
Did she go home already?

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:57.750
-I'm done for the day.
-Good night!

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:08.660
Monica!

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:12.950
Monica! Monica! Monica!

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:39.770
Sarah? What is it?

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:42.110
It's Monica.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:45.150
Monica is...

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:08.010
Monica...

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:13.430
Monica has passed away.

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:32.180
Sarah.

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:37.390
It must be difficult.

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:50.780
It was her birthday.

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:56.410
There's so much
I still wanted to talk to her about.

00:15:58.160 --> 00:15:59.000
I'm so sorry.

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:14.140
Back when I first joined the prosecution,
she would often scold me.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:16.010
She really looked after me.

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:18.100
I still had...

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:21.180
so much to learn from her.

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:45.080
Where did he go off to?

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:47.080
Are you talking about James?

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:49.420
I didn't realize you knew him.

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:52.420
Monica would talk about him often.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:54.510
I see.

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:58.550
There he is.

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:01.600
James.

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:04.190
This is...

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:06.190
the infamous...

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:11.690
I'm Sarah. Sarah Sinclair.
I heard a lot about you from Monica.

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:13.950
Sarah worked with Monica.

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:16.410
She talked about you as well.

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:20.080
I'm James Blood.

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:24.000
I can't count the number of times
she's had to help me.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:29.500
Without her...

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:35.340
I wouldn't be where I am today.

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:38.840
I still can't believe she's gone.

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:41.180
She was too young.

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:45.520
I wasn't done bothering her.

00:17:50.310 --> 00:17:53.690
Monica really took care of the two of you.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:58.530
The cause of death was heart failure.

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:03.290
She really was too young.

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:13.420
What is it?

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:15.800
When Monica...

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:20.050
There was something unnatural
about the way Monica collapsed.

00:18:21.350 --> 00:18:23.060
I'm sorry for putting it that way.

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:26.930
It's hard to express in words.

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:29.940
It's like she was swallowed by the crowd.

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:30.940
From the festival.

00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:34.570
And also, she...

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:37.950
She was carrying a bag!

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:39.910
But it was gone.

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:44.290
My memory is a bit vague
from all the confusion, but...

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:47.160
Have you told anyone else this?

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:49.500
No, I didn't have definite proof.

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:56.460
But I've been constantly reliving
the last moments of her life

00:18:56.550 --> 00:18:58.170
over the last few days.

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:01.340
And I couldn't shake
this unsettling feeling.

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:03.510
-Which is?
-She collapsed.

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:07.270
No, she was knocked over.
In other words...

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:09.520
She was killed?

00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:18.820
It may just be my imagination...

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:21.740
but I couldn't accept the alternative.

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:26.490
Was she working on something dangerous?

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:32.000
I don't know, she never shared very much
about her own work.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:36.500
But I've been allowed
to organize her desk.

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:39.630
I was hoping I might find something.

00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:52.850
Sarah, if you find anything,
I want you to reach out to the SSC.

00:19:58.070 --> 00:19:58.900
Thank you.

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.620
We'll need to look into this right away.

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:18.210
It's been too long. You've done quite well
for yourselves, haven't you?

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:21.840
What I've made is nothing compared to you.

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:23.430
Pardon me.

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:42.090
Monica...

00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:44.510
What were you mixed up in?

00:22:32.470 --> 00:22:33.390
Come on!

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:05.130
I figured the surveillance footage
would be a dead end.

00:23:06.170 --> 00:23:09.050
It's almost impossible
to tell anyone apart in this crowd.

00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:17.730
James?

00:23:18.020 --> 00:23:18.930
<i>What is it, Sarah?</i>

00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:21.350
There's something I want you to see.

00:23:23.560 --> 00:23:25.110
Okay, I'll...

00:23:27.070 --> 00:23:28.360
I'm already on my way.

00:23:29.530 --> 00:23:31.820
James, James, James.

00:23:58.350 --> 00:23:59.220
James.

00:24:19.540 --> 00:24:22.040
Subtitle translation by Zensho Yamamoto
